sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant C as Caller (Executor / MarketData / GEX)
    participant Q as PriorityQueue
    participant W as dispatchLoop (writer)
    participant RL as RateLimiter + Breaker
    participant D as Deribit
    participant R as readLoop (reader)

    C->>Q: Call(method, params, priority) → Enqueue (deadline = now + 30 s)
    W->>Q: Next() — high lane first
    W->>W: drop if deadline passed (never send a stale order)
    W->>RL: Wait(pool by method) · breaker check (skipped for high priority)
    W->>W: register pending[id] + timeout timer
    W->>D: write frame
    Note over W: the writer moves on — it never waits for the reply
    D-->>R: response {id, result | error}
    R->>R: takePending(id) → stop timer
    alt business rejection (e.g. price_too_low)
        R->>RL: breaker Success (exchange is healthy)
    else exchange unhealthy (10028, 11051, 13888 …)
        R->>RL: breaker Failure
    end
    R-->>C: reply on the caller's channel

    opt read-only method rate-limited
        C->>Q: retry with full-jitter backoff (orders are never retried)
    end

    Note over R,D: connection drops
    R->>R: cancel connection goroutines
    R-->>C: every in-flight call fails fast with ErrConnectionLost
    R->>R: reconnect(rootCtx): backoff, dial, auth, re-subscribe
    alt reconnect attempts exhausted
        R-->>C: Gateway.Fatal() → main shuts down, supervisor restarts, reconcile rebuilds state
    end
